+# R3 barrier mapping and scope
+
+No commits/push/branches/worktree/PR/staging/index/merge/tag/release/deploy, remote messages or remote mutations. Local owned fixtures only.
+
+Original `r3-baseline-probes.cjs` and `check-r3-probes.py` are immutable copies of reviewer bytes. `baseline24.jsonl` is the complete named134ecd baseline on Node24.22.1:14 cases,7 desired failures, baseline checker0, desired checker1. Initial Node26 measurement is preserved separately and is not Node24 evidence.
+
+| Original barrier/oracle | Mapped barrier/oracle | Control proving execution |
+|---|---|---|
+| L recovery before mutable-path rename; second recovery then replacement acquire | First recovery holds the shared mkdir mutex at the actual quarantine rename; second recovery AND acquire return7. First finishes0; replacement acquire then succeeds; old handle release returns8 and leaves replacement nonce intact. The original interleaving is excluded by the protocol. `result` records the blocked competing recovery, `first` records the owning recovery; no silent relabelling as the old first recovery. | `hits=1`, first0, competing7, acquire `lock_protocol_busy`, stale release `lock_owner_changed`, actual fresh owner file matching nonce. Independent actual-FS deferred-barrier tests also cover release. |
+| Early cancel at `fsyncDir(lock)` while acquiring | After protocol guard removal/root sync, with usable owner published and before apply admission | One hit, APT0/0/0 before request, exit130, target events empty. The old callback now executes inside the protocol mutex and cannot recursively publish. |
+| C-late fourth version-lock read | Version-lock read in real `finalPlanAdmission`, still before first intent/effect | Stack-selected barrier and one hit; APT0/0/0 before request and at exit130; journal empty. No-cancel counterpart completes all three operations once. |
+| Second writer writes directly to final cancel file, partial JSON/ENOSPC | Actual reserved temp `payload` write, partial JSON/ENOSPC before file fsync and rename | First durable accepted request hash retained; one fault hit, product typed8 `lock_transition_unconfirmed`, consumer still matches. Suite additionally injects fsync/rename/parent-fsync faults. |
+| Cancel legacy target_* fields | Internal v2 full owner object | Strict generation match; mapped checker reads v2 owner PID/nonce. Full boot/start/installation/time identity and foreign/new-generation controls run in suite. |
+| Raw ENOSPC escapes | Fault is translated into typed transition8 | Exact product code checked, injected partial write hit required, before/after hashes equal. |
+| R211 recover0/repeat0 despite prepared review | recover8/repeat8 `context_review_unproven`, `review_required:true`, `resume_authorized:false`; resume8 then explicit review/resume0 | Exact direct/plan-first ordered cases; effects before=after, checkpoint retained, no auto review. Original runner/checker bytes and historical raw red retained. |
